#{[17592186431877 #edb/ref 1080 "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=3u(t)-v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &={u}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186431877 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431877 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ae08dcf3-62ce-5a52-845e-1dd4af782784" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431883 #edb/ref 1080 "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=3{u}^{2}(t)-{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=4u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186431883 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431883 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f0064606-8a67-5c4c-866a-5588c435a49b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186431883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431885 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431885 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431885 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186431874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431885 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "11f2b70f-bcb2-5554-a4f5-52982774bf66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431889 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431889 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335386" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431889 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431889 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+6y(t)-12 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &={x}^{2}(t)+2x(t)+y(t)-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. An equilibrium point of the system is $[1,\\,3]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting this equilibrium to the origin?" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186431889 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a1db4f53-42d8-55c9-8ba8-b7dde90ef735" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431889 #edb/ref 1074 "To shift the system’s equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,u=\\begin{bmatrix}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,⇒\\,x=u+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn coordinate form, this can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nx(t)=u(t)+1,\\,y(t)=v(t)+3,\\,{x}^{′}(t)={u}^{′}(t),\\,{v}^{′}(t)={y}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now substitute these into the given system.\n\n- Substituting into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =3x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+6y(t)-12 \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =3(u(t)+1)-(v(t)+3)^{2}+6(v(t)+3)-12 \\\\  & =3u(t)+3-({v}^{2}(t)+6v(t)+9)+6v(t)+18-12 \\\\  & =3u(t)-{v}^{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substituting into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{2}(t)+2x(t)+y(t)-6 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =(u(t)+1)^{2}+2(u(t)+1)+(v(t)+3)-6 \\\\  & =({u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+1)+2u(t)+2+v(t)+3-6 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)+4u(t)+v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=3u(t)-{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &={u}^{2}(t)+4u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552903 #edb/ref 1080 "The shifted system has exactly one equilibrium point." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552903 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552903 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "13f81b54-2c42-5068-ae9b-f58486c9e0ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552947 #edb/ref 1080 "\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t)=-2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552947 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218